update public.species set body = $v$Spends its time just below the surface waiting for small insects, so a tight-fitting lid is essential, as it can launch itself out of the water. Keep a group and offer floating foods. Peaceful but easily startled.$v$ where slug = $v$silver-hatchetfish$v$;
update public.species set body = $v$Pairs jump together to deposit eggs above the waterline, then the male splashes them to keep them wet. It is extraordinary behavior. Peaceful and best with a tight lid and floating plants. Keep a small group.$v$ where slug = $v$splash-tetra$v$;
update public.species set body = $v$Often confused with the very similar Rosy Tetra, and the two are frequently mixed up in the trade. Keep a school of 6 or more in soft, slightly acidic water with plants. Males flare at each other but rarely do harm, and they suit most peaceful communities.$v$, scientific_name = $v$Megalamphodus bentosi$v$, genus = $v$Megalamphodus$v$, former_names = array[$v$Hyphessobrycon bentosi$v$]::text[] where slug = $v$ornate-tetra$v$;
